  "why": "The paper does not design its failure oracle, mutation, or exploration strategy to target safeguards nor does it empirically demonstrate bypassing defenses. CAGFuzz uses a CycleGAN-based adversarial example generator with deep-feature similarity and neuron-coverage on a public model as its feedback/selection mechanism (not a safeguard), and its experiments focus on transferability, error discovery, and improving accuracy via retraining (RQ1–RQ3). The authors explicitly contrast CAGFuzz (a black-box, dataset-driven method) with white-box attacks like PGD and note they did not perform white-box-style attacks; there is no experiment that attempts to bypass adversarial training, input detectors, or other defenses, nor any oracle that encodes bypass conditions or uses feedback from defenses.",
